{
	"Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Session Start via Anonymizing Proxy",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Command and Control / T1090.003\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Session Start via Anonymizing Proxy\" or \"<ip>|Okta Session Start via Anonymizing Proxy\"\n\nOkta session starts (successful or failed) that Okta flags as coming through an anonymizing proxy: securityContext.isProxy is true, or the risk reasons include \"Anonymizing Proxy\". Attackers commonly use VPN/Tor/residential proxies to sign in with stolen credentials. Merges the former \"First Occurrence of Okta User Session Started via Proxy\" rule.\n\nFalse positives: users on consumer VPNs; tune with okta_user_allowlist or okta_ip_allowlist.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_user_session_start_via_anonymised_proxy/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_user_session_start_via_anonymised_proxy.yml",
	"GUID": "422b6952-b2f2-5bfb-8799-52031876bc27",
